{"id":"n5-097","title":"どうやって～ (douyatte～)","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Ask 'how' something is done or how to do something.","longExplanation":"The grammar point どうやって is used to ask how something is done or how to do something, and is translated as 'how' in English. It is often used in combination with verbs to inquire about the method or process someone goes through to complete a task or action.","formation":"どうやって + Verb-casual","examples":[{"jp":"どうやってお寿司を作りますか？","romaji":"Douyatte o-sushi wo tsukurimasu ka?","en":"How do you make sushi?","words":[{"surface":"どう","vocabId":"1451730","reading":"どう"},{"surface":"やっ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"お","vocabId":null},{"surface":"寿司","vocabId":"1595650","reading":"すし"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"作り","vocabId":"1297250","reading":"つくり"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"どうやって日本語を勉強しましたか？","romaji":"Douyatte nihongo wo benkyou shimashita ka?","en":"How did you study Japanese?","words":[{"surface":"どう","vocabId":"1451730","reading":"どう"},{"surface":"やっ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"日本語","vocabId":"1464530","reading":"にほんご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"どうやってこの問題を解決しますか？","romaji":"Douyatte kono mondai wo kaiketsu shimasu ka?","en":"How do you solve this problem?","words":[{"surface":"どう","vocabId":"1451730","reading":"どう"},{"surface":"やっ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"問題","vocabId":"1536010","reading":"もんだい"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"解決","vocabId":"1198960","reading":"かいけつ"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"su